{"id":"mahabharata-12-249","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":249,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशदधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 249 · Brahma's anger and the woman of death","summary":{"en":"Sthanu, Shiva, begs Brahma to take back the fire of his wrath, which was burning all beings, and Brahma is moved. From the fire a dark woman, Death, comes out of all his openings and Brahma gathers her tears in his hands for the good of men.","kn":"ಬ್ರಹ್ಮನ ಕೋಪಾಗ್ನಿ ಎಲ್ಲ ಜೀವಿಗಳನ್ನು ಸುಡುತ್ತಿರುವುದರಿಂದ ಅದನ್ನು ಹಿಂತೆಗೆದುಕೊಳ್ಳಲು ಶಿವ ಸ್ಥಾಣು ಬೇಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಕರಗುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಆ ಅಗ್ನಿಯಿಂದ ಅವನ ಎಲ್ಲ ದ್ವಾರಗಳಿಂದ ಕಪ್ಪು ಸ್ತ್ರೀ ಮೃತ್ಯು ಹೊರಬರುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಮನುಷ್ಯರ ಹಿತಕ್ಕೆ ಬ್ರಹ್ಮ ಅವಳ ಕಣ್ಣೀರನ್ನು ಕೈಯಲ್ಲಿ ಹಿಡಿಯುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"स्थाणु शिव ब्रह्मा से अपने क्रोध की उस अग्नि को लौटा लेने की प्रार्थना करते हैं जो सब प्राणियों को जला रही थी, और ब्रह्मा पिघलते हैं। उस अग्नि से श्यामा स्त्री मृत्यु उनके सब द्वारों से निकलती है और ब्रह्मा मनुष्यों के हित में उसके आँसू हाथों में थाम लेते हैं।","te":"బ్రహ్మ కోపాగ్ని అన్ని జీవులను కాల్చడంతో దాన్ని ఉపసంహరించమని స్థాణువు శివుడు వేడుకుంటాడు; బ్రహ్మ కరుగుతాడు. ఆ అగ్ని నుండి అతని అన్ని ద్వారాల నుండి నల్లని స్త్రీ మృత్యువు వెలువడుతుంది, మనుషుల హితం కోసం బ్రహ్మ ఆమె కన్నీళ్లను చేతిలో పట్టుకుంటాడు.","ta":"பிரம்மனின் சினத்தீ எல்லா உயிர்களையும் எரிப்பதால் அதைத் திரும்பப்பெறுமாறு ஸ்தாணு சிவன் வேண்ட, பிரம்மன் மனமிரங்குகிறான். அத்தீயிலிருந்து அவன் எல்லா வாயில்களிலும் கருநிறப் பெண் மரணம் வெளிப்படுகிறாள், மனிதர் நலனுக்காக பிரம்மன் அவள் கண்ணீரைக் கைகளில் ஏந்துகிறான்.","ml":"സ്ഥാണു എന്ന ശിവൻ, ജീവികളെ ദഹിപ്പിക്കുന്ന തന്റെ കോപാഗ്നി തിരിച്ചെടുക്കാൻ ബ്രഹ്മാവിനോട് അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു; ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അലിയുന്നു. ആ അഗ്നിയിൽനിന്ന് കറുത്ത സ്ത്രീയായ മൃത്യു അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ എല്ലാ ദ്വാരങ്ങളിൽനിന്നും പുറത്തുവരുന്നു; മനുഷ്യരുടെ നന്മയ്ക്കായി ബ്രഹ്മാവ് അവളുടെ കണ്ണീർ കൈകളിൽ ശേഖരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.249; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"स्थाणुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sthanu said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रजासर्गनिमित्तं मे कार्यवत्तामिमां प्रभो ।\nविद्धि सृष्टास्त्वया हीमा मा कुप्यासां पितामह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord, understand that I came on account of the creation of beings; these were made by you, grandfather, so do not be angry with them."}},{"n":2,"text":"तव तेजोग्निना देव प्रजा दह्यन्ति सर्वशः ।\nता दृष्ट्वा मम कारुण्यं मा कुप्यासां जगत्प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"God, all creatures are burning in the fire of your radiance; seeing them I am moved to compassion. Lord of the world, do not be angry at them."}},{"text":"प्रजापतिरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Prajapati said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"न कुप्ये न च मे कामो न भवेरन्प्रजा इति ।\nलाघवार्थं धरण्यास्तु ततः संहार इष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am not angry and I do not wish that creatures should not exist; but for the sake of lightening the earth, destruction is wanted."}},{"n":4,"text":"इयं हि मां सदा देवी भारार्ता समचोदयत् ।\nसंहारार्थं महादेव भारेणाप्सु निमज्जति ॥","meaning":{"en":"This goddess, afflicted by her burden, always urged me toward destruction, Mahadeva, for she sinks in the waters under the weight."}},{"n":5,"text":"यदाहं नाधिगच्छामि बुद्ध्या बहु विचारयन् ।\nसंहारमासां वृद्धानां ततो मां क्रोध आविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When I could not find, by much thinking with my intellect, any way to destroy these multiplied creatures, then anger entered me."}},{"text":"स्थाणुरुवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sthanu said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"संहारान्तं प्रसीदस्व मा क्रुधस्त्रिदशेश्वर ।\nमा प्रजाः स्थावरं चैव जङ्गमं च विनीनशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Be gracious, lord of the thirty gods, and do not be angry; do not destroy creatures, moving or unmoving."}},{"n":7,"text":"पल्वलानि च सर्वाणि सर्वं चैव तृणोलपम् ।\nस्थावरं जङ्गमं चैव भूतग्रामं चतुर्विधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the pools and all the grass and shrubs, the moving and unmoving, the fourfold host of beings,"}},{"n":8,"text":"तदेतद्भस्मसाद्भूतं जगत्सर्वमुपप्लुतम् ।\nप्रसीद भगवन्साधो वर एष वृतो मया ॥","meaning":{"en":"all this world has been turned to ash and is flooded. Be gracious, good lord; this is the boon I have chosen."}},{"n":9,"text":"नष्टा न पुनरेष्यन्ति प्रजा ह्येताः कथंचन ।\nतस्मान्निवर्त्यतामेतत्तेजः स्वेनैव तेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Once lost, these creatures will never come back; therefore withdraw this fire with your own radiance."}},{"n":10,"text":"उपायमन्यं संपश्य प्रजानां हितकाम्यया ।\nयथेमे जन्तवः सर्वे निवर्तेरन्परंतप ॥","meaning":{"en":"For the good of creatures, find another means by which all these beings may be turned back, scorcher of foes."}},{"n":11,"text":"अभावमभिगच्छेयुरुत्सन्नप्रजनाः प्रजाः ।\nअधिदैवनियुक्तोऽस्मि त्वया लोकेष्विहेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without birth, creatures would come to an end; lord, you appointed me over the divine realm in the worlds."}},{"n":12,"text":"त्वद्भवं हि जगन्नाथ जगत्स्थावरजङ्गमम् ।\nप्रसाद्य त्वां महादेव याचाम्यावृत्तिजाः प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lord of the world, the world, moving and unmoving, is born of you. Having pleased you, Mahadeva, I beg that creatures be born again and again."}},{"text":"नारद उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Narada said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"श्रुत्वा तु वचनं देवः स्थाणोर्नियतवाङ्मनाः ।\nतेजस्तत्स्वं निजग्राह पुनरेवान्तरात्मना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Sthanu's words, the god, with speech and mind controlled, drew back his own fire into himself."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततोऽग्निमुपसंगृह्य भगवाँल्लोकपूजितः ।\nप्रवृत्तिं च निवृत्तिं च कल्पयामास वै प्रभुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having withdrawn the fire, the venerable lord, honoured by the worlds, established activity and withdrawal."}},{"n":15,"text":"उपसंहरतस्तस्य तमग्निं रोषजं तदा ।\nप्रादुर्बभूव विश्वेभ्यः खेभ्यो नारी महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he withdrew that fire born of anger, from all the openings of the great one a woman appeared."}},{"n":16,"text":"कृष्णा रक्ताम्बरधरा रक्तनेत्रतलान्तरा ।\nदिव्यकुण्डलसंपन्ना दिव्याभरणभूषिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was dark, wore red garments, had red-cornered eyes, wore divine earrings and was adorned with divine ornaments."}},{"n":17,"text":"सा विनिःसृत्य वै खेभ्यो दक्षिणामाश्रिता दिशम् ।\nददृशातेऽथ तौ कन्यां देवौ विश्वेश्वरावुभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming out of the openings she went to the southern direction. The two gods, lords of the universe, looked at the maiden."}},{"n":18,"text":"तामाहूय तदा देवो लोकानामादिरीश्वरः ।\nमृत्यो इति महीपाल जहि चेमाः प्रजा इति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Calling her, the god, first lord of the worlds, said, \"Death! Kill these creatures.\""}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वं हि संहारबुद्ध्या मे चिन्तिता रुषितेन च ।\nतस्मात्संहर सर्वास्त्वं प्रजाः सजडपण्डिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You were conceived by my thought of destruction, in my anger; therefore destroy all creatures, fools and wise alike.\""}},{"n":20,"text":"अविशेषेण चैव त्वं प्रजाः संहर भामिनि ।\nमम त्वं हि नियोगेन श्रेयः परमवाप्स्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Destroy creatures without distinction, lovely lady. By carrying out my order you will attain the highest good.\""}},{"n":21,"text":"एवमुक्ता तु सा देवी मृत्युः कमलमालिनी ।\nप्रदध्यौ दुःखिता बाला साश्रुपातमतीव हि ॥","meaning":{"en":"So addressed, the goddess Death, wearing a lotus garland, grew sad and pensive, and wept bitterly."}},{"n":22,"text":"पाणिभ्यां चैव जग्राह तान्यश्रूणि जनेश्वरः ।\nमानवानां हितार्थाय ययाचे पुनरेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of men took those tears in his hands, and again begged her for the good of humankind."}}]}]}